              "call_781f612ed1ab487982af0cef96a0cb6b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Whole-parent searches locate the affected modules' direct imports in architectures.py. Its imports are unconditional, whereas the inspected package initializers export Config and Model without directly importing that registry. Thus the demonstrated shared failure boundary is registry loading, including Config.from_directory, rather than necessarily the initial root-package import.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a8902d06a32c4af7a811bc2be672e220",
              "call_51b1436909bd42daa712ba15eb09d09d",
              "call_fa850b3d1f5a4848bd861aa951167abc",
              "call_4018ddc49fcf4eb8bd7e0d532e43f370",
              "call_5c6051b5884148f2917bc0b10e7c374d",
              "call_c1b82199e6134116ae5cab56f517c6ec",
              "call_6ff0a96b805c43358d353f5487a5b706"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Using the backport unconditionally avoids a version-dependent import branch and follows the surrounding models' convention. This is a compatibility interpretation of the narrow diff, not measured proof that every supported interpreter can load the package.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_997071d2985a45e2b7185fc76f835414",
              "call_933a0b0e27934d308410e89df78040c8",
              "call_24439aea84224d2f97c8c82e9796ecca",
              "call_3e652c8cda82403d9882b0136fb6c294"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
